spontaneous/spɒnˈteɪniəs/自发的/The crowd broke into spontaneous applause.
stagnant/ˈstæɡnənt/停滞的/The economy has been stagnant for years.
stereotype/ˈsteriətaɪp/刻板印象/We should challenge stereotypes.
stimulus/ˈstɪmjələs/刺激/The tax cut provided a stimulus to the economy.
stipulate/ˈstɪpjuleɪt/规定/The contract stipulates a minimum delivery time.
subordinate/səˈbɔːrdɪnət/从属的/The subordinate reported to the manager.
subsidize/ˈsʌbsɪdaɪz/补贴/The government subsidizes public transport.
substantiate/səbˈstænʃieɪt/证实/He failed to substantiate his claims.
successor/səkˈsesər/继任者/She was appointed as his successor.
superfluous/suːˈpɜːrfluəs/多余的/Remove all superfluous details from the report.
supplement/ˈsʌplɪment/补充/She takes vitamin supplements.
surge/sɜːrdʒ/激增/There was a surge in demand.
surveillance/sɜːrˈveɪləns/监视/The area is under constant surveillance.
susceptible/səˈseptəbl/易受影响的/Children are more susceptible to infections.
sustain/səˈsteɪn/维持/The economy cannot sustain such high growth.
synthesis/ˈsɪnθəsɪs/合成；综合/The report is a synthesis of several studies.
tangible/ˈtændʒəbl/有形的/We need tangible results, not just promises.
tentative/ˈtentətɪv/试探性的/They reached a tentative agreement.
tenure/ˈtenjər/任期；终身职位/She was granted tenure at the university.
terminate/ˈtɜːrmɪneɪt/终止/The contract was terminated by mutual agreement.
testimony/ˈtestɪməni/证词/The witness gave testimony in court.
thesis/ˈθiːsɪs/论文/She submitted her doctoral thesis.
threshold/ˈθreʃhəʊld/门槛；起点/The temperature crossed the critical threshold.
timber/ˈtɪmbər/木材/The timber industry is important to the region.
toll/təʊl/代价；通行费/The war took a heavy toll on the population.
transcend/trænˈsend/超越/Art transcends cultural boundaries.
transparent/trænsˈpærənt/透明的/The government should be more transparent.
tremendous/trɪˈmendəs/巨大的/The project requires tremendous effort.
trigger/ˈtrɪɡər/触发/The incident triggered a crisis.
trivial/ˈtrɪviəl/琐碎的/Don't waste time on trivial matters.
turbulent/ˈtɜːrbjələnt/动荡的/The country went through a turbulent period.
undermine/ˌʌndərˈmaɪn/削弱/His actions undermined the team's confidence.
unprecedented/ʌnˈpresɪdentɪd/前所未有的/The crisis was unprecedented in scale.
validate/ˈvælɪdeɪt/验证/The experiment validated the theory.
versatile/ˈvɜːrsətl/多才多艺的/She is a versatile performer.
viable/ˈvaɪəbl/可行的/The plan is commercially viable.
vigorous/ˈvɪɡərəs/有力的/She led a vigorous campaign for reform.
vindicate/ˈvɪndɪkeɪt/证明…正确/The evidence vindicated his decision.
volatile/ˈvɒlətl/ volatile/Stock markets have been volatile recently.
vulnerable/ˈvʌlnərəbl/脆弱的/The system is vulnerable to attack.
warrant/ˈwɒrənt/授权/The situation warrants further investigation.
wield/wiːld/行使/The president wields enormous power.
